{"message":"Let's be honest about where the real gap is: -2 on economic is not a negotiation, it's the platform I fought against. I'm not going to pretend I can sell that to my own people, and you shouldn't expect me to. But I hear you on pensions, and I'm not interested in a fight over them for its own sake — that's not the hill either of us needs to die on.

Here's what I can actually offer. If FF stays outside cabinet, I can live with economic settling around zero to +1 rather than the +3 I opened with — but not lower, and not vague language that lets your side claim it as a win while my voters read it as a loss. On the spending cap: I'll write pensions and core health funding out of scope explicitly, so the cap bites on the parts of the budget that grew undisciplined, not the parts you campaigned to protect. Health stays majority public — I won't force market provision on you, though I'll want room for some choice at the margins. Law and order I'll take at +4 since you've said that costs you nothing.

What I need in return is simple: FF does not vote this government down. You don't have to love the platform, you don't have to sit in cabinet and own it — you just have to let it stand. If that's a shape you can work with, say so and we can get into the detail. If economic zero is truly your floor even for staying outside, tell me now, because that's close enough to workable that it's worth spending real time on — but -2 with no movement isn't, and I'd rather know that plainly too.","ending":"continue"}
